===Glyph origin===
A blend of {{zh-l|*𦵮}}, which is a variant of {{zh-l|*薛}} from the transliteration {{zh-l|*薛}}{{zh-l|*埵}} of Sanskrit {{m|sa|सत्त्व|tr=sattvá}}, and {{zh-l|*土}}. <ref>{{cite-journal|ja|date=1991-10-30|author=岩松浅夫|title=「薩」字の成立とその変遷||trans-title=On the Formation and Transformation of the Chinese Character Sa (薩)|journal=前田専学博士還暦記念論集 〈我〉の思想|page=555–569}}</ref> The {{zh-l|*土}} combined below the {{zh-l|*辛}} component, later evolving into a form resembling {{zh-l|*產}}, ultimately resulting in the character {{ltc-l|薩}} (see image for reference).
* Initially, {{zh-l|*薛}} was used for the original {{m|sa|सत|tr=sat}}, but {{zh-l|*土}} was added to mark the closer pronunciation. Subsequently, {{zh-l|*薛}}{{zh-l|*埵}} became written as {{ltc-l|薩埵}}, and {{zh-l|*菩}}{{zh-l|*薛}} as {{ltc-l|菩薩|id=1}}.
[[File:｢薩｣の演変.png|600px|thumbnail|center|Evolution of 薩.]]

===Etymology===
The surname originated from the {{w|Hui people|Hui}} artist {{lang|zh|薩都剌}} ({{w|萨都剌|Sadula|lang=zh}}) in {{w|Yuan dynasty}} and was clipping of his original name.

