From {{inh|ja|ojp|sort=あい|-}}, from {{inh|ja|jpx-pro|sort=あい|*awoy}}.

There are various theories regarding the ultimate derivation, all suggesting a relation to {{ja-r|青|あを|rom=awo → ao|[[blue]]}}:
* May be an alteration from {{ja-r|青%色|あを%いろ|rom=awoiro → aoiro}}:
*: {{IPAfont|⟨awoiro<sub>2</sub>⟩}} → {{IPAchar|/awoirə/}} → {{IPAchar|/awɨrə/}} → {{IPAchar|/airo/}} → {{IPAchar|/ai/}}
* May be a fusion of {{ja-r|青|あを|rom=awo → ao}} and {{ja-r|い|pos=emphatic particle}}:<ref>Thomas Pellard (2013). [https://hal.archives-ouvertes.fr/hal-01289288/document Ryukyuan perspectives on the proto-Japonic vowel system]. Frellesvig, Bjarke; Sells, Peter. Japanese/Korean Linguistics 20, CSLI Publications, pp.81–96, 2013.</ref>
*: *{{IPAchar|/awo i/}} → *{{IPAchar|/awɨ/}} → *{{IPAchar|/awi/}} → *{{IPAchar|/aji/}} → {{IPAchar|/ai/}}
* May be derived from a compound of {{ja-com|sort=あい|青|あを|rom1=awo → ao|居|ゐ|rom2=wi → i|t2=[[there is]]}}, expressing the sense that the indigo plant ''contains'' the color blue:
*: {{IPAchar|/awowi/}} → *{{IPAchar|/awːɨ/}} → {{IPAchar|/awi/}} → *{{IPAchar|/aji/}} → {{IPAchar|/ai/}}

